Subject: RE: [geomorph-r-package] Factorial Nested ANOVA?
Message-ID: <QxvaUFKF9Dk.Lbu3UJcbFwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <QxvaUFKF9Dk.LY3cvHQaFwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <QxvaUFKF9Dk.LY3cvHQaFwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/QxvaUFKF9Dk/m/Lbu3UJcbFwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Milena,

If by tree you mean those that grow in the forest (as opposed to phylogenetic trees), then yes you can.  For a nested model where B is nested within A:

procD.lm(Y~A/B)

See the help page for advanced.procD.lm for an example in geomorph.

Dean

