Hi Milena,

It is possible to run this something similar to this model, and then use nested.update twice, in succession, to update the F values for the A and C effects.  For example,

fit <- procD.lm(Y~A/B + C/B)

fit <- nested.update(fit, ~A/B)
fit <- nested(update(fit, ~C/B)

You can also try

> procD.lm(Y~ (A*C)/B)

But I do not believe the nested.update function would be useful - it is not capable of handling such complex designs.

Mike

